# Campaign: Complete supervised loop history and milestone release continuity

Status: completed
Type: campaign
Updated: 2026-09-04
Roadmap: PRM-0039
Roadmap Revision: 3
Milestones: M3-SUPERVISED-HISTORICAL-REVIEW, M4-HOSTED-OPERATIONS-AND-RETENTION
Required Endpoint: Work2

## Outcome

Provide a revision-bound supervised historical review that resolves only explicitly reviewed
findings, retain resolved and recurrence history without replay actions, and permit sequential
milestone releases while the owning roadmap remains honestly open.

## Completion Gate

- Historical audit supports bounded sources and active/resolved history.
- Exact per-finding or complete-lineage manifests fail closed on stale state or omitted findings.
- Guarded apply records each reviewed decision and re-audits local authority.
- Resolved dashboard history is bounded and has no action control.
- A released milestone cohort no longer blocks a later Work2 cohort under the same open roadmap.
- Focused local, dashboard, reporter, checkpoint/rebuild, Linux, Windows, and development-web
  evidence passes for the exact candidate.

## Completion Evidence

- Historical review manifest `work/evidence/loop-history-review-m3-v0.45.0.json` resolved the
  three inherited findings through explicit, revision-bound decisions; the fresh audit reports
  zero active and three resolved findings.
- Candidate commit `877de11f2cd8206828c3162a34639b4e2406ed57` passed the release validation
  profile (579 tests) and the development web, Linux, and Windows lanes recorded in release-lane
  manifest `07e467d8-ffd8-45b7-9dbc-e70ac62112a3`.
- The hosted projection retains bounded resolved history without copy actions, while sequential
  milestone cohorts preserve released history and permit one later mutable cohort.
